== G. Width, font, accessibility
  OLD page: 390 -> scrollWidth 390 / clientWidth 390; Figtree not used (document.fonts.check('600 16px Figtree') = false)
  NEW page: 390 -> 390 / 390, 1280 -> 1280 / 1280, 600 -> 600 / 600; success card 390 -> 390 / 390; select list open at 390 -> 390 / 390
            (first measure open at 390 gave 396: the search box of the select list; fixed with overflow: hidden on .select2-search--dropdown)
  Figtree: document.fonts.check('600 16px Figtree') = true on every new capture
  contrast: label 14.5, help note 6.7, warning note 5.5, field error 6.1, required mark 5.0, button 5.0, placeholder 4.6 (all >= 4.5)
  Tab order: name, type, acronym, country, website, send; every stop shows a 2 px brand outline (select lists included after a fix:
            an outline:none on the focused select box beat the focus-visible rule)

